		<title type="html"><![CDATA[MD-UV390 &quot;Helicoptering&quot; Tx Audio on DMR Nets]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4988&amp;p=36349#p36349"><![CDATA[
I've got an MD-UV390 GPS unit and tried using it with my Heil HTH-K headset w/boom mic.  Tx &amp; Rx audio are fine using FM analog.  Rx audio is fine on DMR, but Tx audio is reported as having a strong 'helicoptering' effect.  This has happened on multiple DMR nets I've tried it on.  However, if I plug it into my Anytone 878 sitting right next to the 390, the Tx audio is clear.  So it seems it's an issue with the 390, not necessarily the headset.  I did try adding ferrite beads at both ends of the headset cable, with virtually no effect on the distortion.<br>Any thoughts on what's going on?  Might there be a setting in the 390 I can adjust that might fix this?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5794">W3ATN</a> — Sat Mar 22, 2025 1:30 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
